Assistant: I see the issue. We're trying to use Jest's mocking functionality, but Jest isn't available in this environment. Let's modify the preview file to use a different approach for mocking the components:

<file path="apps/web/.temp/dessn-component-routes/Page-b8e77f64.tsx">
<change>
<description>Remove Jest mocking and use direct component overrides</description>
<content>
import React, { Suspense } from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';

// Mock the required components and functions
const mockComponents = {
  SettingsHeader: ({ title, description, children }: { title: string; description: string; children: React.ReactNode }) => (
    <div className="settings-header">
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p>{description}</p>
      {children}
    </div>
  ),
  
  FlagListingView: () => (
    <div className="flag-listing-view">Mock Flag Listing View</div>
  ),
};

// Mock the translation function
const getTranslate = () => {
  return (key: string) => key;
};

// Mock the metadata generator
const _generateMetadata = async (titleFn: (t: any) => string, descriptionFn: (t: any) => string) => {
  return {
    title: titleFn((key: string) => key),
    description: descriptionFn((key: string) => key),
  };
};

// Override the imports that the component will use
const mockImports = {
  '@calcom/features/flags/pages/flag-listing-view': {
    FlagListingView: mockComponents.FlagListingView,
  },
  '@calcom/features/settings/appDir/SettingsHeader': mockComponents.SettingsHeader,
  'app/_utils': {
    getTranslate,
    _generateMetadata,
  },
};

// Add mocks to global scope
if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
  (window as any).__mocks__ = mockImports;
  (window as any).getTranslate = getTranslate;
  (window as any)._generateMetadata = _generateMetadata;
}

// Create the preview component
export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({});

  return (
    <div className="preview-wrapper">
      <mockComponents.SettingsHeader 
        title="Feature Flags" 
        description="Admin Flags Description"
      >
        <mockComponents.FlagListingView />
      </mockComponents.SettingsHeader>
    </div>
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

I've made several changes to fix the error:

1. Removed all Jest-related code since it's not available in this environment
2. Created a simpler mock implementation that directly renders the mocked components
3. Simplified the component structure by removing the async wrapper since we can directly render the mocked components
4. Added the mocks to the window object in a more straightforward way
5. Rendered the components directly instead of trying to import the actual page component

The changes:
- Remove Jest mocking
- Use direct component rendering with mocks
- Simplify the overall structure
- Remove async complexity
- Provide a more stable preview environment

This should resolve the "jest is not defined" error while still providing a meaningful preview of the component.

